Because `ThumbnailMaker` is abstract and no concrete subclasses are provided in the context, we must use an anonymous subclass to instantiate it. (Note: The exact abstract methods of `ThumbnailMaker` are not shown in the context, so a dummy `make` method is inferred based on standard library patterns).

